 @page documentation_tarch_visualisation_pyvista Explore data with PyVista
 
 <a href="https://docs.pyvista.org/">PyVista</a> is popular with Peano, as a 
 lot of end users prefer Python for postprocessing, or even want to embed the
 postprocessing into Jupyter notebooks.
 
 # Installation

 As with the rest of Peano's Python side, install into a virtual environment
 rather than into your system Python - @ref page_installation_home
 "consult the installation page" if you have not set one up for Peano yet:

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 python3 -m venv .venv
 source .venv/bin/activate
 pip install --upgrade pip
 pip install -e .
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 PyVista itself is not part of Peano's own `requirements.txt` - it is an
 optional, purely postprocessing-side dependency - so install it into that
 same virtual environment on top:

 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 pip install pyvista
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 Remember to run `source .venv/bin/activate` again in every new terminal
 session before you use PyVista.

 # Using PyVista
 
